  "body": "PR1552's complete reset graph passes a separately implemented chronological audit. This package checks **all 1,431 intervals in four dirty-state contexts**, including **1,325 intervals absent from every supplied complete schedule**. It corroborates the existing 31-point frontier; no discrepancy or new construction is claimed.\n\n**Status: independent finite verification; no new kappa or selected-supplier adoption.** Only `research/independent-reset-graph/` is added.\n\nThe verifier imports no predecessor executable. It reconstructs interval entry states by executing the eager echo and its literal inverse, independently emits the fixed child/return words, propagates sparse exact operators and solves suffix costs. This provides separate evidence for losing edges as well as the winning words. PR1552 already supplies its own Fraction-column frontier replay and small controls; those checks and the mathematical result retain their credit.\n\nReproduce with Python 3.12 and the standard library:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/independent-reset-graph\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_INDEPENDENT_RESET_GRAPH`, `PASS_RESET_AUDIT_PACKAGE`, then `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=completed`.\n\nCoverage includes 5,724 contextual interval executions, all 1,017 width thresholds, 2,052 exact published distance entries, and 40 full schedule records containing 33 distinct words. Both directions' dirty maps, integer-grid halvings, instruction hashes, access counts and maximizing sign inputs are checked. All 255 partitions of a separate two-pair fixture agree with 86 direct cap decisions. Ten mathematical controls include an unused-edge corruption and a nonmaximal-context corruption invisible to the recorded maximum. Three on-disk corruptions reject; read-only relocation and deterministic regeneration pass.\n\nLocal registered Python 3.12.13 replay passes. Optimized Python 3.14.6 produces a byte-identical audit receipt. Metadata/source pins and whitespace checks pass; the clean patch applies to refreshed main `680967accfd4311f3241dc154e1f434869747b43`. Hosted CI, full selected cold replay, physical/rounded admission and formal or independent human review are separate, unclaimed checks.\n\nBase: `64039f1bd3b6a523b96083fd858ad040a75e3030`; OS assignment seed **59**, recursive interfaces. The final overlap refresh found concurrent PR1552, prompting one pivot from the duplicate construction to this complete-graph verification. It also found PR1563, which changes the root word by cancelling a terminal return pair; its extended graph is outside this audit. The selected frontier and `upstream/` are unchanged.\n\nExact sources: PR1552 `4db7213c90288b1eb83983e08c5ef401d19b7844`; Sagar Thakrar's PR1537 `407f00df6ca0bf86b455b5640f18ec2f62ee77b9`. Immutable source bytes, Git blobs and hashes are retained. Credit the concurrent Hanson Sun PR1552 contribution for the canonical frontier, Sagar Thakrar for the fixture and paid return, and Ross Richardson's PR1287 plus PR1227/889/1203 lineage for the frame/echo mechanisms.\n\nPrepared for **Hanson Sun (@bbMisk)** with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance** in derivation, code, checking and prose. Source and audit are separate AI-assisted sessions under the same account; implementation independence is as described, not independent human review. Apache-2.0. The README records inherited assumptions and concrete open questions. No merge or closure is requested.\n",
